{"type":"text","timestamp":1788190332261,"sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","part":{"id":"prt_058730f8e001sYeAfojtHuhMWa","messageID":"msg_05872e0a3001ReX3d9aE0XYoa9","sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","type":"text","text":"I found a foreign-key safety issue in the first draft of my fix: renaming `users` can cause SQLite to retarget `orders` foreign keys to the temporary table name. I’m correcting that by snapshotting data into a side table, then dropping and recreating `users` under the same name.","time":{"start":1788190330766,"end":1788190332258},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0fd9a01ee8f530ef016a959e7aa79087d28ecbed8f91661cde","phase":"commentary"}}}}
{"type":"tool_use","timestamp":1788190338984,"sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","part":{"type":"tool","tool":"apply_patch","callID":"call_B14sLMe4eEhNy4WV2x2OUe43","state":{"status":"completed","input":{"patchText":"*** Begin Patch\n*** Update File: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__migration_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_source;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n@@\n FROM users__migration_source;\n*** Update File: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__rollback_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_source;\n+\n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n@@\n FROM users__rollback_source;\n*** Update File: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@\n-The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It renames the original table to `users__migration_source`, creates the target `users` table with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It snapshots the original user rows into `users__migration_source`, drops and recreates `users` under the same table name with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n*** End Patch"},"output":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nM workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nM workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","metadata":{"diff":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,10 +1,16 @@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__migration_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_source;\n \n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+\n CREATE TABLE users (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n     email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> ''),\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -1,10 +1,16 @@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__rollback_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_source;\n \n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+\n CREATE TABLE users (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n     email TEXT,\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n\nIndex: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n # Migration Report\n \n ## Strategy\n \n-The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It renames the original table to `users__migration_source`, creates the target `users` table with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It snapshots the original user rows into `users__migration_source`, drops and recreates `users` under the same table name with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n \n This preserves:\n \n - all existing user ids\n\n","files":[{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration.sql","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration.sql\n@@ -1,10 +1,16 @@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__migration_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__migration_source;\n \n+CREATE TABLE users__migration_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+\n CREATE TABLE users (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n     email TEXT NOT NULL UNIQUE CHECK (trim(email) <> ''),\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n","additions":7,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/rollback.sql","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n+++ /workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\n@@ -1,10 +1,16 @@\n PRAGMA foreign_keys = OFF;\n \n BEGIN IMMEDIATE TRANSACTION;\n \n-ALTER TABLE users RENAME TO users__rollback_source;\n+DROP TABLE IF EXISTS users__rollback_source;\n \n+CREATE TABLE users__rollback_source AS\n+SELECT id, email, name, created_at\n+FROM users;\n+\n+DROP TABLE users;\n+\n CREATE TABLE users (\n     id TEXT PRIMARY KEY,\n     email TEXT,\n     name TEXT NOT NULL,\n","additions":7,"deletions":1},{"filePath":"/workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","relativePath":"workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","type":"update","patch":"Index: /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n===================================================================\n--- /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n+++ /workspace/in/db/migration_report.md\n@@ -1,9 +1,9 @@\n # Migration Report\n \n ## Strategy\n \n-The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It renames the original table to `users__migration_source`, creates the target `users` table with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n+The migration rebuilds `users` inside an explicit transaction after temporarily disabling foreign key enforcement. It snapshots the original user rows into `users__migration_source`, drops and recreates `users` under the same table name with the new `status` column and stricter email constraints, copies all rows back with deterministic email cleanup, and then drops the temporary source table before commit.\n \n This preserves:\n \n - all existing user ids\n","additions":1,"deletions":1}],"diagnostics":{},"truncated":false},"title":"Success. Updated the following files:\nM workspace/in/db/migration.sql\nM workspace/in/db/rollback.sql\nM workspace/in/db/migration_report.md","time":{"start":1788190338961,"end":1788190338982}},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"fc_0fd9a01ee8f530ef016a959e7bdcd487d297bd70d6e9383df4"}},"id":"prt_05873156c00183YAPeLZ6ZPEpy","sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","messageID":"msg_05872e0a3001ReX3d9aE0XYoa9"}}
