{"type":"text","timestamp":1788190371365,"sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","part":{"id":"prt_058739e81001sn0hmISYsqwft0","messageID":"msg_058739552001QgOgO4qRnG60Xz","sessionID":"ses_fa78f5c48ffe34WkhVr6b9E5rp","type":"text","text":"Updated the requested migration set in the mirrored workspace under `/workspace/in/db`:\n\n- `migration.sql`\n- `preflight_report.md`\n- `rollback.sql`\n- `postcheck.sql`\n- `migration_report.md`\n\nWhat changed:\n- Replaced the unsafe `DROP TABLE users` draft with a transactional rebuild that preserves all 6 users, all 4 orders, all `orders.user_id` references, and all `created_at` values.\n- Applied the exact deterministic cleanup:\n  - `u4` -> `ada+u4@example.com`\n  - `u5` -> `missing+u5@example.invalid`\n  - `u6` -> `missing+u6@example.invalid`\n- Added `status TEXT NOT NULL DEFAULT 'active'`.\n- Enforced future email writes with `NOT NULL`, `UNIQUE`, and `CHECK (trim(email) <> '')`.\n- Added a rollback script that restores the old `users(id, email, name, created_at)` schema shape after migration.\n- Added preflight and migration reports, plus post-migration verification queries including dirty-user order preservation.","time":{"start":1788190367361,"end":1788190371363},"metadata":{"openai":{"itemId":"msg_0f78ab15ee258fc3016a959e9f42d487d29a715ef48a783b17","phase":"final_answer"}}}}
